# Build output.
/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.tmp

# Nested build trees. Agent worktrees and any hand-made worktree carry
# their own `target/`, which `/target` (anchored at the repo root) does
# not cover. Without these, a worktree under the repo leaks a few GB of
# object files into `git status`.
**/target/
/worktrees/
/.worktrees/

# Local agent state — track only the shared bits.
#
# `.claude/*` excludes the *contents* of the directory rather than the
# directory itself, which is what makes the re-includes below work: git
# will not descend into an excluded directory, so `.claude/` (with the
# trailing slash and no star) would make `!.claude/skills/` silently
# dead and drop the repo-scoped skills from version control.
#
# Tracked: `skills/` (docs-sync, push — they travel with the codebase)
# and `settings.json` (shared project config, if one is ever added).
# Untracked: `settings.local.json`, `worktrees/`, and anything else
# personal to one machine.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
.kiro/*
!.kiro/skills/
!.kiro/settings.json

# Editor and OS state.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.orig
*.rej

# Local environment. `.env` can hold credentials; none of it is
# reproducible from the repo.
.env
.envrc
.direnv/

# Planning / analysis docs written during a working session. These are
# working notes, not part of the published contract — the README and
# CHANGELOG are. Keep them on disk, out of the repo.
/framework_integration.md
/*_plan.md
/*-plan.md

# Python tooling caches.
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Python extension build products.
#
# The compiled module is scoped to where maturin puts it rather than a
# bare `*.so`: an unanchored rule would also swallow a vendored grammar
# or a test fixture anywhere in the tree, silently, and this repo already
# vendors parser sources under `crates/cgg-lang/vendor/`.
/crates/cgg-py/python/cgg/*.so
/crates/cgg-py/python/cgg/*.pyd
/crates/cgg-py/python/cgg/*.dylib
/dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# Node build products. `index.js`/`index.d.ts` ARE generated by the napi
# CLI, but they are committed on purpose: they are the package's entry
# point and its public type surface, and reviewing a change to them is
# how an accidental API change gets noticed.
node_modules/
/crates/cgg-node/*.node
/crates/cgg-node/npm/*/*.node
